+{"rule_id":"draftly-rule-commonlii-LKSC-2004-23-1","statement_correct":false,"quote_supports":true,"is_ratio":true,"qualifications_ok":false,"statute_correct":true,"usable":false,"reason":"The holding concerned money lent without written security repayable on demand, so the statement is overbroad without that limitation."}
+{"rule_id":"draftly-rule-commonlii-LKSC-2004-25-1","statement_correct":false,"quote_supports":false,"is_ratio":false,"qualifications_ok":false,"statute_correct":true,"usable":false,"reason":"The court held that no particular public purpose had been claimed and that section 39A divesting did not require proving ultra vires, not a general rule that the Minister's claim must specify the purpose."}
+{"rule_id":"draftly-rule-commonlii-LKSC-2004-7-1","statement_correct":false,"quote_supports":false,"is_ratio":false,"qualifications_ok":false,"statute_correct":true,"usable":false,"reason":"The statement is malformed and omits that the actual holding placed the section 66(1) Trusts Ordinance burden on the transferee."}
+{"rule_id":"draftly-rule-commonlii-LKSC-2004-7-2","statement_correct":false,"quote_supports":false,"is_ratio":false,"qualifications_ok":false,"statute_correct":true,"usable":false,"reason":"The court decided a specific burden of proof under section 66(1), while the statement's reference to legal responsibility is too vague and inaccurate."}
+{"rule_id":"draftly-rule-commonlii-LKSC-2005-11-1","statement_correct":false,"quote_supports":false,"is_ratio":true,"qualifications_ok":false,"statute_correct":true,"usable":false,"reason":"The majority held that the estate date of death should be 21.04.1988 under the amended presumption, not the tautological date of death itself."}
+{"rule_id":"draftly-rule-commonlii-LKSC-2005-17-1","statement_correct":true,"quote_supports":true,"is_ratio":true,"qualifications_ok":false,"statute_correct":true,"usable":false,"reason":"The broad deega-forfeiture proposition is supported, but the statement drops the listed modes by which binna rights may be reacquired."}
+{"rule_id":"draftly-rule-commonlii-LKSC-2005-5-1","statement_correct":true,"quote_supports":true,"is_ratio":false,"qualifications_ok":false,"statute_correct":true,"usable":false,"reason":"This is mainly a fact-specific appellate conclusion on the particular corpus and omits the burden and kurakkan-sowing qualifications."}
+{"rule_id":"draftly-rule-commonlii-LKSC-2005-7-1","statement_correct":true,"quote_supports":true,"is_ratio":true,"qualifications_ok":true,"statute_correct":true,"usable":true,"reason":"The court used the strict-construction rule for taxing statutes to resolve doubt in favour of the Bank as taxpayer."}
+{"rule_id":"draftly-rule-commonlii-LKSC-2006-16-1","statement_correct":true,"quote_supports":true,"is_ratio":false,"qualifications_ok":false,"statute_correct":true,"usable":false,"reason":"The statement gives only the Act's purpose and omits the operative holding that section 18 includes buildings on state land."}
+{"rule_id":"draftly-rule-commonlii-LKSC-2006-5-1","statement_correct":true,"quote_supports":true,"is_ratio":true,"qualifications_ok":true,"statute_correct":true,"usable":true,"reason":"The court held that the substance of the instrument must be examined to decide whether it is a bond."}
+{"rule_id":"draftly-rule-commonlii-LKSC-2006-5-2","statement_correct":true,"quote_supports":true,"is_ratio":true,"qualifications_ok":false,"statute_correct":true,"usable":false,"reason":"The statement is supported for the documents before the court but omits the fixed-sum and bond-character conclusion that made the point legally material."}
+{"rule_id":"draftly-rule-commonlii-LKSC-2006-5-3","statement_correct":true,"quote_supports":true,"is_ratio":true,"qualifications_ok":true,"statute_correct":true,"usable":true,"reason":"The court held that an instrument under seal binding payment of a specified sum can include guarantee and indemnity bonds."}
+{"rule_id":"draftly-rule-commonlii-LKSC-2006-6-1","statement_correct":false,"quote_supports":true,"is_ratio":true,"qualifications_ok":false,"statute_correct":true,"usable":false,"reason":"The holding was confined to first examining whether partition land was commonly owned under section 2(1), not preliminary issues generally."}
+{"rule_id":"draftly-rule-commonlii-LKSC-2006-6-2","statement_correct":false,"quote_supports":true,"is_ratio":true,"qualifications_ok":false,"statute_correct":true,"usable":false,"reason":"The dismissal power was tied to a partition action where the land had ceased to be commonly owned, not any action whenever land is dividedly possessed."}
+{"rule_id":"draftly-rule-commonlii-LKSC-2006-6-3","statement_correct":true,"quote_supports":true,"is_ratio":true,"qualifications_ok":true,"statute_correct":true,"usable":true,"reason":"The statement captures one stated limb of the court's holding on adverse possession between co-owners."}
+{"rule_id":"draftly-rule-commonlii-LKSC-2007-1-1","statement_correct":true,"quote_supports":true,"is_ratio":true,"qualifications_ok":true,"statute_correct":true,"usable":true,"reason":"The court treated relaxed pleading as applicable where equality infringement was alleged from unlawful high-level executive benefits."}
+{"rule_id":"draftly-rule-commonlii-LKSC-2007-1-2","statement_correct":true,"quote_supports":true,"is_ratio":true,"qualifications_ok":true,"statute_correct":true,"usable":true,"reason":"The court accepted public-interest standing to seek a declaration that wrongful executive benefits breached equality before the law."}
+{"rule_id":"draftly-rule-commonlii-LKSC-2007-1-3","statement_correct":false,"quote_supports":false,"is_ratio":true,"qualifications_ok":false,"statute_correct":true,"usable":false,"reason":"The statement reverses the court's formulation, which said organs of government are temporary custodians while power remains reposed in the people."}
+{"rule_id":"draftly-rule-commonlii-LKSC-2007-14-1","statement_correct":false,"quote_supports":false,"is_ratio":false,"qualifications_ok":false,"statute_correct":true,"usable":false,"reason":"The statement is too vague and omits that the requirement was fraud or collusion under section 7(2) of the Registration of Documents Ordinance."}
+{"rule_id":"draftly-rule-commonlii-LKSC-2007-14-2","statement_correct":false,"quote_supports":false,"is_ratio":true,"qualifications_ok":false,"statute_correct":true,"usable":false,"reason":"The fraud-or-collusion requirement applied to defeating prior registration under section 7(2), not to succeeding in civil cases generally."}
+{"rule_id":"draftly-rule-commonlii-LKSC-2007-14-3","statement_correct":true,"quote_supports":true,"is_ratio":true,"qualifications_ok":true,"statute_correct":true,"usable":true,"reason":"The court stated and applied the higher civil probability required for fraud as compared with negligence."}
+{"rule_id":"draftly-rule-commonlii-LKSC-2007-3-1","statement_correct":false,"quote_supports":false,"is_ratio":false,"qualifications_ok":false,"statute_correct":true,"usable":false,"reason":"The statement is truncated and records only that reliefs were examined, not the court's legal holding."}
+{"rule_id":"draftly-rule-commonlii-LKSC-2007-3-2","statement_correct":true,"quote_supports":true,"is_ratio":true,"qualifications_ok":false,"statute_correct":true,"usable":false,"reason":"The statement is correct but omits the material reason that the two sets of relief were linked by the same bank resolution and procedural steps."}
+{"rule_id":"draftly-rule-commonlii-LKSC-2007-3-3","statement_correct":true,"quote_supports":true,"is_ratio":true,"qualifications_ok":true,"statute_correct":true,"usable":true,"reason":"The court applied the principle that courts may lift the corporate veil in appropriate circumstances, including improper use to defeat creditors."}
+{"rule_id":"draftly-rule-commonlii-LKSC-2008-2-1","statement_correct":true,"quote_supports":true,"is_ratio":true,"qualifications_ok":true,"statute_correct":true,"usable":true,"reason":"The court used these common corporate characteristics in deciding that the Sri Lanka Transport Board lacked body-corporate status under the Act."}

